    "turn_text": "Oh, well, there's a lot of ex post facto rationalisation there where he's accused of things that happened after the revolution took place. There are a lot of things that he's accused of that actually had been around for 150 years since the founding of the American colonies. There are some things like the bit about him taking people across the oceans for punishment when nobody was taken across any ocean at all. No American was taken across any ocean at all for punishment. So there's a lot of padding, you know, lawyers padding. It's a propaganda document from a wartime. It's perfectly understandable why Jefferson was trying to do that. However, the two key ones, the 17th charge about taxation and the 22nd charge about Parliament's veto rights over American legislation do in and of themselves justify the American Revolution.",
